            <ArticleTitle>[Aneurysmal vertebra cyst (observation on two cases with neurological findings) (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>633-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report 2 cases of aneurysmal cysts of the spinal cord with neurological manifestations. The first case was a young girl of 16 years of age with a lesion at the D6 level and spasmodic paraparesis. The second case was a boy aged 5 years with a lesions at the L3 level and lumbar pains. The characteristic &quot;one-eyed vertebra&quot; appearance was present in the radiological images in both cases, and was confirmed histologically on operation, which produced good results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
